confirmed successor status cancelled.\n- Actual intake_after_merge probe with the adopted queued WI-020 carrying needs=[\"WI-005\"]. Summary: \"dropped queued/WI-020-successor.md's edge(s) WI-005\"; intake returned ([], None); adopter needs changed from WI-005 to empty.\n- Exported ccd66391996fd1669d666e3f9ade235163081de9's shipped code and tests with git archive into the review directory, overlaid only current test_handback.py/test_intake.py, and ran python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider -n 0 --basetemp C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-10-11-leg03/pre-fix-test-temp tests/test_handback.py::test_an_adoption_of_a_superseding_row_closes_and_sweeps tests/test_intake.py::test_an_unreadable_merged_adjudication_spec_refuses_the_sweep tests/test_intake.py::test_a_title_match_off_the_drafts_lineage_refuses_the_mint. Summary: 5 failed, 1 warning in 6.74s; adoption acceptance, unreadable-spec refusal and both title-collision cases are red on pre-fix behavior.\n- Invoked the current drafts-only late-dependent replay regression against that same pre-fix export. Summary: assertion failed at test_intake.py:1643 after the real replay; subsequent registry inspection confirmed WI-030 still needed WI-005. Thus the enduring drafts-only regression also detects the pre-fix defect.\n- snapshot_probe.py over the scoped amended rows. Summary: system-requirements.toml True; low-level-requirements.toml True; test-cases.toml True (live versus approved snapshot equality).\n\nFindings:\n- [MAJOR] project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py:1801 -> K1/B1: existence of the completed disposition at before is treated as proof its adoption was successfully consumed. On a real repository the landing sweep rejects an already-terminal successor, but a later bare sweep calls _landed_before with HEAD, skips the open-state rule, returns 0 and redirects the dependent to that rejected successor; reproduced for both complete and cancelled successors. This contradicts SR-148's already-open successor acceptance and LLR-335/TC-360's first-consumption guarantee, and makes recovery silently erase the refusal -> Replace file-existence replay eligibility with acceptance evidence bound to the exact adoption, produced only by successful consumption at the owning sweep boundary; retain SR-148 acceptance/approval and IF-244's refusal contract, carry the corrected replay semantics and rejected-then-replayed regression into LLR-335/TC-360 and re-attest the changed child content. This is the structural producer fix called for by .agents/skills/antidote/SKILL.md, rather than an additional compensating open-state guard -> @kit-builder\n- [MINOR] docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml:3454 -> K1, for clarity: LLR-335 says neither consumer changes the adopted registry row's own cells, but the real sweep's shared lineage pass removes that row's needs edge to the disposed item; an accepted queued WI-020 with needs=[\"WI-005\"] finished with empty needs. That rewrite is consistent with successor dependency semantics, while the blanket no-cell-change claim is false -> Narrow the claim to adoption validation leaving the successor's identity, scope and Supersedes unchanged, explicitly allowing the shared needs rewrite; re-attest LLR-335 and synchronize its approval snapshot, retaining SR-148's acceptance and TC-360's behavioral obligations -> @kit-builder\nVERDICT: CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=2","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73ae5cf9-d335-4bb7-a08f-7631da597f26","uuid":"8701593b-c712-4e79-8c43-8453167d6167","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:12:46.720Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Reviewed: 4a8e7f64ce4ee0bd2733a7829b7cd51ae872d859\n\nVerified: Independently read the specified three-dot authored diff, CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md, PROCESS.md, WI-902's full spec and handback.py SpecRef, rubric, and cited requirement/test/interface rows. Hunted silent successor misbinding, fail-open acceptance, and destructive dependency rewrites first. Valid adoption closes and sweeps wi